C# classes are reference types, so mutation is natural. Change return types from entity types to void.

**Pattern for entity diffs:**
```csharp
// BEFORE:
public static Type ApplyTypeDiff(Type baseType, TypeDiff diff) {
    var result = new Type { Guid = baseType.Guid, Name = diff.Name ?? baseType.Name, ... };
    return result;
}

// AFTER:
public static void ApplyTypeDiff(Type target, TypeDiff diff) {
    if (diff.Name != null) target.Name = diff.Name;
    // ... etc for each field
}
```

**Pattern for collection diffs:**
```csharp
// BEFORE:
public static IEnumerable<Type> ApplyTypesDiff(IEnumerable<Type> items, TypesDiff diff) {
    var result = items.ToList();
    // ... filter, select, add
    return result;
}

// AFTER:
public static void ApplyTypesDiff(List<Type> items, TypesDiff diff) {
    if (diff.Removed != null) {
        var removedGuids = new HashSet<string>(diff.Removed.Select(r => r.Guid));
        items.RemoveAll(i => removedGuids.Contains(i.Guid));
    }
    if (diff.Updated != null) {
        foreach (var update in diff.Updated) {
            var item = items.FirstOrDefault(i => i.Guid == update.TypeId.Guid);
            if (item != null) ApplyTypeDiff(item, update.Diff);
        }
    }
    if (diff.Added != null) {
        items.AddRange(diff.Added);
    }
}
```

Note: The Kit's collection properties may use `IEnumerable<T>`. For in-place mutation, they need to be `List<T>`. You may need to change the Kit class properties from `IEnumerable<T>` to `List<T>` or ensure they are backed by lists.

**Pattern for ApplyKitDiff:**
```csharp
// BEFORE:
public static Kit ApplyKitDiff(Kit baseKit, KitDiff diff) {
    var result = new Kit { Guid = baseKit.Guid, Name = diff.Name ?? baseKit.Name, ... };
    return result;
}

// AFTER:
public static void ApplyKitDiff(Kit kit, KitDiff diff) {
    if (diff.Name != null) kit.Name = diff.Name;
    if (diff.Version != null) kit.Version = diff.Version;
    // ... scalar fields
    if (diff.Types != null) {
        if (kit.Types == null) kit.Types = new List<Type>();
        var typesList = kit.Types as List<Type> ?? kit.Types.ToList();
        ApplyTypesDiff(typesList, diff.Types);
        kit.Types = typesList;
    }
    // ... etc for all collections
}
```

#### 3. Update ALL Callers

```csharp
// BEFORE:
var result = ApplyKitDiff(baseKit, diff);

// AFTER:
ApplyKitDiff(baseKit, diff);
// baseKit is now mutated
```

For tests needing originals, use `DeepClone()`:
```csharp
var clone = DeepClone(kit);
ApplyKitDiff(clone, diff);
```

